      en: "The James Norman Hall Home in Arue, Tahiti, was the residence of the American writer who co-authored the bestseller 'Mutiny on the Bounty' with Charles Nordhoff. Hall settled in Tahiti in 1935 and lived in this house until his death in 1951. The building is a traditional Polynesian house with a wooden veranda and corrugated iron roof. Today it is a museum displaying Hall's life, works, and his relationship with Tahiti. It houses personal items, manuscripts, and photographs.",
